<title>USA: Norton McNaughton sees breakeven Q2.</title>
<headline>Norton McNaughton sees breakeven Q2.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norton McNaughton Inc said Monday it expects breakeven results for the fiscal second quarter, begun February 2, compared with a loss of $0.09 per share a year earlier.</p>
<p>During the second half of fiscal 1997, it expects continuing improvements in gross margin and increasing profitability due to solid performance of its products at retail &quot;as we launch a more fashionable and wider product assortment,&quot; the company said.</p>
</text>
